      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of the number \\(24\\), we first need to find its prime factorization.\n\nThe prime factorization of \\(24\\) is:\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nThe formula to find the number of positive divisors of a number \\(n\\) with the prime factorization \\(n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k}\\) is:\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nFor the number \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\), the exponents are \\(3\\) and \\(1\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\\[\n(3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of \\(24\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
