      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of the number \\(24\\), we first need to find its prime factorization.\n\n1. **Prime Factorization of \\(24\\):**\n   \\[\n   24 \\div 2 = 12 \\\\\n   12 \\div 2 = 6 \\\\\n   6 \\div 2 = 3 \\\\\n   3 \\div 3 = 1\n   \\]\n   So, the prime factorization of \\(24\\) is:\n   \\[\n   24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Using the Formula for the Number of Divisors:**\n   If a number \\(n\\) has a prime factorization of the form:\n   \\[\n   n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k}\n   \\]\n   then the number of positive divisors of \\(n\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Applying the Formula to \\(24\\):**\n   For \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   e_1 = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad e_2 = 1\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the number of positive divisors is:\n   \\[\n   (3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n   \\]\n\n4. **List of Positive Divisors:**\n   The positive divisors of \\(24\\) are obtained by taking all possible products of the prime factors raised to their respective powers. They are:\n   \\[\n   1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of positive divisors of \\(24\\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
